#. ja: マッドスキッパー
#. de: Schlammspringer
#. fr: poisson grenouille
#. column 2: mudskippers
#. column 8: An amphibious fish which can survive for bells out of water as long as its skin remains moist. When on land, the mudskipper uses its pectoral fins to “wander” about in search of shelter. Because of this trait, the fish is sometimes associated with the god Oschon.<br><br>[Suitable for printing on small canvases.]
#. column 9: Mudskipper
msgctxt "Item:4939:0:0"
msgid "mudskipper"
msgstr "илистый прыгун"

